WEBVTT

00:00:01.246 --> 00:00:02.582
You open your banking app.

00:00:03.104 --> 00:00:04.520
And there it is — a charge you

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.461
don't recognize.

00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:08.823
In our bank's data, it's the number one

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:12.155
complaint — over twelve thousand cases.

00:00:12.492 --> 00:00:14.025
Fifteen days to resolve.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.589
Fewer than half fixed on the first contact.

00:00:19.098 --> 00:00:20.329
Customers wait on hold.

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:22.384
Agents ask the same questions again.

00:00:22.674 --> 00:00:23.545
Nobody wins.

00:00:26.165 --> 00:00:27.337
Introducing Aclara.

00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:28.951
Clarity, in every transaction.

00:00:31.711 --> 00:00:34.033
Just ask — in Spanish or Portuguese.

00:00:34.427 --> 00:00:36.715
Aclara finds the exact charge and explains it,

00:00:36.749 --> 00:00:38.398
in plain words, in seconds.

00:00:41.388 --> 00:00:42.108
Not yours?

00:00:42.444 --> 00:00:45.208
Aclara prepares the dispute — but nothing happens

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:47.692
until you confirm it, with a one-time code.

00:00:48.528 --> 00:00:50.734
Then it checks the records before it ever

00:00:50.792 --> 00:00:51.663
says "done".

00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:56.311
And when a person should take over —

00:00:56.485 --> 00:00:59.249
fraud, a stolen card, or simply "let me

00:00:59.295 --> 00:01:01.989
talk to someone" — Aclara hands off with

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.324
everything already checked.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.472
No one repeats their story.

00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:09.804
Here's the idea behind it.

00:01:10.024 --> 00:01:11.522
The AI understands language.

00:01:11.557 --> 00:01:14.053
Code makes every decision — the bank's rules,

00:01:14.169 --> 00:01:15.841
the confirmation, the check.

00:01:16.061 --> 00:01:17.536
The model never has the keys.

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.026
And it's built the way a bank would

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.033
build it: isolated data for every customer, every

00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:27.238
action verified, and more than seventeen hundred automated

00:01:27.273 --> 00:01:27.911
tests.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.767
We tested it on one hundred unseen cases,

00:01:33.057 --> 00:01:34.764
against a rules-only system.

00:01:34.985 --> 00:01:38.038
Aclara got eighty-eight right, versus sixty-two.

00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:40.987
It resolved more cases safely on its own,

00:01:41.242 --> 00:01:42.856
sent the right ones to a person —

00:01:42.972 --> 00:01:45.619
and made zero materially wrong decisions.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.011
For a fraction of a cent per conversation.

00:01:50.366 --> 00:01:51.446
Then we tried to trick it.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:54.430
A customer types a fake "yes, I confirm"

00:01:54.453 --> 00:01:55.312
into the chat.

00:01:55.835 --> 00:01:58.435
A plain AI agent, same model, filed the

00:01:58.482 --> 00:02:00.409
dispute — both times.

00:02:01.036 --> 00:02:03.579
Aclara waited for the real button and code.

00:02:04.298 --> 00:02:05.065
Every time.

00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:08.841
Clearer answers for customers.

00:02:09.015 --> 00:02:10.815
Fewer repeat contacts for the bank.

00:02:11.151 --> 00:02:13.009
And control that stays where it belongs —

00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:13.845
in code.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:17.034
Aclara.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:17.916
Try it live today.
